            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "vivienfanghuagood"
            },
            "body": "Thanks for this. I built this PR's head for gfx1100 and ran the AOT kernel unit tests on a Radeon PRO W7900D (gfx1100). The build and `import sgl_kernel.common_ops` both succeed, but two of the MoE gating kernels fail at runtime:\n\n| test (one pytest per file) | this PR on gfx1100 |\n|---|---|\n| test_moe_topk_softmax | process aborts (`Fatal Python error: Aborted`) |\n| test_moe_topk_sigmoid | `torch.AcceleratorError: HIP error: unspecified launch failure` (first case, `test_topk_sigmoid[1-4-1]`) |\n| test_activation | 945 passed |\n| test_apply_token_bitmask_inplace | 1 passed |\n| test_topk | 118 passed |\n| test_dsv4_norm_rope | 16 passed |\n| test_moe_align | 4368 passed, 72 skipped |\n\nThe cause is the warp size. `include/utils.h` defines `WARP_SIZE` as 64 in the host pass and 32 in the gfx11 device pass. `topkGatingSoftmax` / `topkGatingSigmoid` are launched with `dim3 block_dim(WARP_SIZE, WARPS_PER_TB)` and with template constants derived from the host value, while the kernel bodies assume 32 lanes. The same failures reproduce on gfx1201 (R9700) with only the allowlist widened on current `main`.\n\nThe fix already exists on `amd_march` as #44600 (mixed wave32/wave64 AOT kernels). With that change ported onto current `main` plus the allowlist, all of the tests above pass on both gfx1100 and gfx1201:\n\n- topk_softmax 744 passed\n- topk_sigmoid 774 passed\n- topk 164 passed, 1 skipped\n\nTwo smaller points:\n\n- `main` has since lowered the non-gfx942 TopK dynamic-smem budget to 40 KB, which already fits gfx1100's 64 KB LDS. The 48 KB change is optional now.\n- This PR is based on a September `main`, and `setup_rocm.py` has moved since.\n\nMerged as is, this would ship a kernel that imports fine but faults or mis-routes on MoE models. We've proposed the full RDNA kernel-build change (allowlist for gfx110x/gfx120x plus the #44600 launch fix) in #46900, along with a question to the AMD maintainers about RDNA CI, which they asked for before RDNA lands on `main`. I'd suggest closing this in favour of that, or rebasing it on that change. Happy to help either way.",
